# Context uploaded by `gcloud builds submit`. Without this file, gcloud falls back on .gitignore —
# which would be enough today, but would make the non-leaking of .env and of the private notes depend
# on a file written for an entirely different reason. The exclusion is therefore explicit here.
#
# Careful: as soon as this file exists, it entirely replaces the fallback on .gitignore. Everything
# that must stay out of the context has to appear here. `tests/` deliberately does not: cloudbuild's
# test step needs it if the build is launched by hand with --config.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
.env
.env.example
*.private.md
CLAUDE.md
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
backend/.llm_budget.json
backend/memory/.seen_items.json
backend/memory/.analyzed_history.json
backend/eval/*.json
scripts/.run_log.jsonl
